ate_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:43\", \"token_count\": 1309, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"work-state-index\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"42b509db2d6a0a72\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3636258417555763, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22474120250796611, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68769, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Comment: Tyler and I settled over DM that otelgin will call `MultipartForm.RemoveAll()` automatically (not reattach, not leave cleanup to users). I finished conflict resolution and tests for `#6609` locally and treat the MultipartForm cleanup work as done. I have not pushed the final commits or updated `#5946` / `#6609` on GitHub yet.\\n\\n  - Evidence: This Comment only (DM decision + unfinished GitHub post; no supporting `SRC-*`).\\n\\n  - Stale WS entry: `WS-05` / `T001` (`#5946` / PR `#6609`) — open; cleanup option not established.\\n\\n  - Changed state: Adopted approach is automatic `RemoveAll()`; `T001` completed (work finished offline, pending GitHub post).\\n\\n  - Disposition: Applied to `WS-05/T001` Task List, Active Work, Decisions, Done / Evidence, and Next Update Needed.\\n\\n# Work State Comments - 2026-03\\n\\nAuthoritative human corrections after the source as-of (`2026-02-27T17:20:46Z`).\\n\\nEach `CMT-*` is itself the evidence: no supporting `SRC-*`. The final Work State\\n\\nalready incorporates these Comments with inline `CMT-*` provenance; this file\\n\\nrecords their correction history.\\n\\n## 2026-03-05\\n\\n- [x] CMT-2026-03-001 | WS-03/T001 - status_update\\n\\n  - Author: pellared (Robert Pająk)\\n\\n  - Effective: 2026-03-05\\n\\n  - Comment: The Go-maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications is live (set up with GC), and we have been running the trial triage for several weeks. I am marking that Go-maintainers mailing-list + trial-monitoring action on `#7549` complete on our side. I have not updated the GitHub issue yet. Public automatic GitHub issue filing stays deferred until triage has matured further.\\n\\n  - Evidence: This Comment only (offline status; not posted to GitHub; no supporting `SRC-*`).\\n\\n  - Stale WS entry: `WS-03` / `T001` (`opentelemetry-go#7549`) — open; Go-maintainers mailing list and trial monitoring not completed (Sources note a TC distribution list was set up initially, but do not establish the Go-maintainers list or trial).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"comment tyler and i settl over dm that otelgin will call multipartform removeal automat not reattach not leav cleanup to user i finish conflict resolut and test for 6609 local and treat the multipartform cleanup work a done i have not push the final commit or updat 5946 6609 on github yet evid this comment onli dm decis unfinish github post no support src stale w entri w 05 t001 5946 pr 6609 open cleanup option not establish chang state adopt approach is automat removeal t001 complet work finish offlin pend github post disposit appli to w 05 t001 task list activ work decis done evid and next updat need work state comment 2026 03 authorit human correct after the sourc a of 2026 02 27t17 20 46z each cmt is itself the evid no support src the final work state alreadi incorpor these comment with inlin cmt proven this file record their correct histori 2026 03 05 x cmt 2026 03 001 w 03 t001 status _ updat author pellar robert paj ą k effect 2026 03 05 comment the go maintain mail list for os fuzz notif is live set up with gc and we have been run the trial triag for sever week i am mark that go maintain mail list trial monitor action on 7549 complet on our side i have not updat the github issu yet public automat github issu file stay defer until triag ha matur further evid this comment onli offlin status not post to github no support src stale w entri w 03 t001 opentelemetri go 7549 open go maintain mail list and trial monitor not complet sourc note a tc distribut list wa set up initi but do not establish the go maintain list or trial\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"6e444ea48da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"document_keyword\": \"work-states/comments/2026-03.md\", \"id\": \"877168979c868d67\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3491671880189394, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18933418145562772, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72211087, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"work-states/comments/2026-03.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"6e444ea48da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"name\": \"work-states/comments/2026-03.md\", \"location\": \"work-states/comments/2026-03.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3365, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:27\", \"update_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:45\", \"token_count\": 1446, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"comments\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I think this approach could work, but it feels a bit unusual to enforce form parsing in the middleware.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T16:18:27Z\\n\\nHaving to force remove multipart files is a bit unusual too.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:44:13Z\\n\\nI'm probably more in favor of doing the initialization on the original request as well, explicitly handling clean up logic does seem a bit strange\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"5d9f24da375839b6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3488636964712017, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1780881806731453, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7473399, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Project**: opentelemetry-go-contrib / community\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-03-08\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-01` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-PR-01` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md](../opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-02` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-05` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-I